    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316-a2">

                <pb facs="0871" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg657"/>


                <head>Mr. Schuchardt to Mr. Nelson</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Commercial Agency</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Piedras Negras,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-07-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 22, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In my communication of June 11 I had the
                    honor to mention to you that a delegation from the Kickapoo reservation, in
                    Kansas, had gone to Santa Rosa to treat with the Kickapoo Indians living in that
                    vicinity, about their removal to the United States, and I offered to communicate
                    to you the result. I have now the honor to inclose, for your information, an
                    original letter on this subject, addressed to me by Mr. Miles, the United States
                    Indian agent, giving a detailed statement of the whole matter. I have also sent
                    several Texas papers, in which you may note the growing excitement in Texas in
                    regard to the depredations committed by Mexicans and Indians living in Mexico.
                    The latest depredations so near San Antonio were perpetrated, in my opinion, by
                    that band of Lipanes and Mescaleros which, a few months ago, was provided by
                    Mexicans on this side of the Rio Grande with ammunition and arms, and as soon as
                    their means of warfare shall be exhausted they will probably again make their
                    appearance in this vicinity, as usual, in order to trade off the plunder brought
                    from Texas for new supplies.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM SCHUCHARDT, <hi rendition="#italic">United States Commercial
                            Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
